From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: cancel the set-gain work on suspend

A gain update queued just before sleep could run into the resume path and
race the first post-wake rumble. Cancel it on suspend with the playback
and stop workers.
---
 drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
index 3d2149c20..1c6852691 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -6164,6 +6164,7 @@ static int haptics_suspend_config(struct device *dev)
 	int rc;
 
 	cancel_work_sync(&chip->global_playback_work);
+	cancel_work_sync(&chip->set_gain_work);
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&chip->stop_work);
 
 	mutex_lock(&play->lock);
